# Architecture

## Layout

- `lib/views/` screens · `lib/viewmodels/` `ChangeNotifier` · `lib/services/` · `lib/models/` · `lib/core/` infra · `lib/app/` wiring
- Entry: `lib/main.dart` → `lib/app/app.dart` (`MultiProvider`)
- Shell: `MainShell` + `MainShellController` / `MainShellTab` (chat=0, goals=1, tasks=2, habits=3, settings=4)

## Data

- Local SQLite (`sqflite`) + sync queue to .NET WebAPI. One `LocalDb.instance` / `DatabaseService` connection to `principles.db` — a second `LocalDb()` deadlocks merge (`database has been locked`). `LocalRemoteExecutor` always enqueues before a live request so bootstrap merge sees in-flight writes. Successful queue items are deleted (not left as `isProcessed`). Habit SQLite `id` is not a server id until `serverId` is set; collision vacates the local-only row. Bootstrap merge indexes the queue once, loads habits/records in bulk, skips unchanged progress, and writes in a few SQLite transactions. It keeps newer/pending local goals, habits, and progress, and prunes server-backed goals/habits/tasks/conversations missing from the snapshot. Profile `LastModified` is `User.UpdatedAt` (not `CreatedAt`). Sync prefers `GET /sync/changes?since=<lastSuccessfulSync>` whenever a cursor exists (including cold start); no cursor uses `GET /sync/bootstrap`. Incremental upsert + `Deleted*Ids` tombstones — never prune by absence on `/changes`. Falls back to full bootstrap when the server sets `RequiresFullBootstrap`, returns 404, or there is no stored cursor. Store the response `ServerTime` as the next `since`. A second pull runs only after local queue items were pushed. Bootstrap/changes include `generalReminders` + `userHabitReminders` (same shape as `GET /reminder/all`, which remains); SyncGate prefers those lists and only falls back to `/reminder/all` on older servers. Habits tab `load()` is local-only by default; remote catch-up is `LaunchDataLoader` / explicit `syncRemote: true`.
- Goals ↔ habits: match by `targetGoalId` or case-insensitive `targetGoal` name (`habitsForGoal` / `habitsUnassignedToGoals` in `habit_progress_viewmodel.dart`). Habits tab is a flat sorted list (goal chips still filter); Goals tab still nests habits under each goal.
- Habit due-on-date uses MAUI computed progress (`YES_AUTO` after frequency is met). SQLite/API store only manual / skip / clear. Lists, Tasks, date-strip fill, and the detail calendar treat auto-filled days as satisfied, not required. Habits-tab “Completed this day” numerator counts only `YES_MANUAL`.
- `DayChangeNotifier` (midnight timer + app resume) refreshes Tasks Today/Tomorrow filters and rolls the Habits date strip to the new today (MAUI `TryAddNewDayColumn` / `OnResume`).
- Task checklists live in `task_subtasks` (owned by parent `taskId`). The parent still carries `Task.subtasks` in memory; sync sends a nested `subtasks` array on `TaskItemDto`. Backend stores them in `tsk.TaskSubtasks` (cascade delete). Completing items does not complete the parent. Repeat copies the list unchecked. Merge keeps local rows when the DTO omits `subtasks`.
- Tasks are user-scoped (not device-scoped). Bootstrap merge upserts `tasks` and removes local server-backed rows missing from that snapshot. `LaunchDataLoader.syncAndHydrate` re-pulls on resume, connectivity, a 3-minute foreground timer, Tasks tab focus, and pull-to-refresh so a Mac/iPhone pair sees each other's work without restarting. Throttled catch-up skips VM re-hydrate; hydrate runs only after a successful remote sync.
- AI Helper chats persist in `ai_conversations` / `ai_messages` (SQLite) and `app.AiConversations` / `app.AiMessages` (server). Client UUID is `clientId`. Empty new chats stay ephemeral until the first user message; after the first assistant reply, `POST /api/ai/title` sets the sidebar title. Hamburger opens the chat history sidebar; sync via queue + bootstrap `conversations`.
- Completing a goal, task, subtask, or habit plays `assets/sounds/complete.wav` and draws the check + burst at the checkbox via `playCompletionCelebration` (on tap). Active/inbox rows stay in place for `kCompletionCelebrationDuration`, then hide (held ids sort as still active so the burst is not left behind; title/overdue chrome stay active until hide). Unchecking is silent.
- Habits tab header tune icon filters by day status (default Not done), on-this-day due (`habitAppliesOnDate`; default Due, also Not due / All), and goal. A just-completed row stays visible for the burst when Not done would hide it.
- Session RAM: habit progress keeps a calendar window (home-widget months), not full `habit_records` (streak scans SQLite separately); Tasks keep active/session-relevant rows and lazy-load Completed; AI chat history lives only in `HelperViewModel.messages`; bootstrap reminder stash is cleared after SyncGate restore.
- Home-screen calendar widgets (Android App Widget + iOS WidgetKit) show scheduled tasks and habits due that day. Flutter publishes JSON via `home_widget` (`HomeWidgetBinder` / `buildHomeCalendarSnapshot`). Sizes: month, week, today. Header arrows and Today stay on-device; `+` and a day open Tasks (`principleswidget://calendar`). iOS needs App Group `group.com.set.principles`.
- Deep links (home-widget taps + local notification taps) share `DeepLinkController` / `DeepLinkAction`. `DeepLinkBinder` + `ReminderService.onNotificationOpened` enqueue; `MainShell` consumes when ready (queued across splash/login). Task → edit sheet; habit → Habit Detail; daily progress reminder (`habits_report` API unchanged for MAUI) → Tasks today. Flutter-only daily reminder UX (Tasks app bar / list menu / glass sheet presets) must not change the shared reminder DTO or `/reminder/habitsreport` contract. Missing target → snackbar. Transient routes/sheets are popped first.
- After sign-in or cold start, `MainShell` shows `SyncGateView` only for full bootstrap (`since` null) or when `since` is ≥ 20 days old (`requiresSyncGate` / `kSyncGateStaleSince`). Recent incremental catch-up paints the shell after `ensureLocalSession` and syncs underneath. While the gate is up it waits for sync (`isBootstrapComplete` / `ensureLoaded`, merge capped at `kBootstrapSyncTimeout`) and reminder restore: inline MAUI why-copy + one permission sheet (`prepareReminderRestore`), then bulk `zonedSchedule` (`applyReminderRestoreJob` on the already-initialized plugin — never a second `initialize`). Without the gate, restore still runs (service dialog for explain if needed). Reminder restore still builds/applies the schedule job when the user denies permission. Road guide auto-starts only after the shell’s first layout settles; first-sync 404/503 Retry/Cancel, deep links, and session remesh wait until the tour is inactive. SyncGate is also skipped when bootstrap and reminder restore already completed this session.
- Server-required actions (Helper chat, habit recommendations, first post-sign-in bootstrap) show MAUI's Error + Retry/Cancel alert on HTTP 404/503 (`serverTechnicalWorkIsInProgress`). Do not show this for offline-capable CRUD. First-sync retry runs after SyncGate (`LaunchDataLoader.retryStartupSyncIfServerDown`).

